<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Gold has climbed further, hitting its high=
est level since mid-May, as traders and investors worry about the outlook f=
or US inflation and bond market jitters.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Spot gold hit almost $4,700 an ounce earli=
er and is now trading at 4,649 an ounce.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Prices jumped last week after the US Treas=
ury Department said it would double its debt purchases of longer-dated bond=
s, as it scrambled to calm the bond market after a sharp rise in yields. Th=
e focus is now on US inflation data and a speech by Federal Reserve chair K=
evin Warsh on Friday for clues on interest rate hikes and the bond market.<=
/p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Cryptocurrencies are also rallying. Bitcoi=
n rose through $80,000 for the first time since May, rising to $80,453 this=
 morning, up more than a quarter in the past week. However the cryptocurren=
cy remains well below the all-time peak of $126,000 reached last year. Ethe=
r also climbed, to $2,503.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Meanwhile in the Middle East, just two com=
modity vessels transited the strait of Hormuz on Monday, the lowest daily t=
ally since early May, with both entering the Gulf, according to shipping da=
ta.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The figure was also well below the 10-day =
average of 14, Reuters reported. However, some ships switch off their navig=
ation transponders on their way through so the real figure could be higher.=
</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Iran said on Monday it had blacklisted 45 =
tankers for violating its rules on passage through the key waterway and thr=
eatened action such as fines against vessels engaging in ship to ship trans=
fers with them.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Oil and stock markets have shrugged off th=
e threat of severe sanctions against Iran or any entity maintaining economi=
c ties with <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Y=
w_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEAWDEn6qGeA7vMnF3ceqAYNFAc6JeUdOBfV=
d7ZoYM2N_qKIyihU1j89ofkRJsjDwnJXsYjMbuAowbk9L6uvGjhmFTzwOR69-kqDVfUt22VrYsz=
mbaiwxF-BMSr3z6DOGigXgNrvqBXNLMVf4XuIIVzQ60tbJmBKwSty-GvkB9VCXGbCjKeKIF5m6T=
zdEuUzbC8/4th/4AriXCnnToa2ZVecOt1aVA/h40/h001.eU0AkKn-3-WYLx7u8Gu2xDrXZIHTR=
7jiYl8v0lzAL-I" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Iran</a> from the US, after nearl=
y six months of war.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Brent crude, the global benchmark, has fal=
len further this morning to $91.41 a barrel, down 76 cents or 0.8%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Asian stock markets are mostly higher, wit=
h Japan=E2=80=99s Nikkei up 0.5% and South Korea=E2=80=99s Kospi rising 0.7=
% while Hong Kong=E2=80=99s Hang Seng dipped 0.15%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Launching what he called Operation Economi=
c Outcast on Monday, the US Treasury secretary, Scott Bessent, called it an=
 unprecedented campaign and compared it with the D-day Normandy landings, a=
 turning point in the second world war.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">However, when asked by a reporter why the =
US wasn=E2=80=99t imposing immediate sanctions, <a href=3D"https://ablink.e=
ditorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR0V6dyckKcatPr3A0ULt=
_lAQbCO-ifGjKm89BIIiVXfLah9xI0zxAnEAnfExlNCq4EHX-pDvQQhvg4t3dgolMtQNfkd67sD=
dSuKqyCEJrokTuXeK3GTMinvyexCiy4xHW2JETuiCch1ZX7T1d6CrTEb_gnEY4BzRrUYsE_4tA2=
nUvLp48B2cZ11lUSSUyrMvbWJwdSVcyRRIbFZBIRXVHo3MS2oE5WHMtukuOgvfQU0yRDIg5pVSa=
6e-d0oJnfWEy4neZ7DUbx5oqadbQRDvXUs/4th/4AriXCnnToa2ZVecOt1aVA/h41/h001.k3w1=
9vbVINIIvFFGpUnABsf0PKM7BWRWhaa76qawCwc" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Bessent =
replied</a>: =E2=80=9CWell, we are giving everyone the opportunity to remed=
y bad behaviour. Why would I want to blow up the global financial system? W=
e believe that it is important to level set and give people a cure period, =
but they should know that that will move very quickly and that we are serio=
us.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It is unclear how far the <a href=3D"https=
://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7f=
IEMgszcCSneHEA1Wh1zgDJGqtA5BLVKex6Nfd1dWxSfMm2Jvm-rAaAsT1scY3nK6vCVZfczgDeQ=
UbZapofetf6BWalwQgA93zbKY731cla5KxxDV0astWumxNaEfCto3D6ghy1gtJMBMI1yyVOyeJG=
P6CQuT57ueTZBGguwmbW6rTh7hp3BQTrJss7P02EIWyZsxf0CamrVb1ATq76nJuiM3QWlBLFjiZ=
9W/4th/4AriXCnnToa2ZVecOt1aVA/h42/h001.O-Rd5bCPp3lSOJM-jz6sHCFoIWMBGaSP9fWn=
DoQPZs4" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Trump administration</a> is prepared to =
go in confronting China, Iran=E2=80=99s biggest trading partner. Tehran <a =
href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_X=
G18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBCzsSoUHqz-djkHPrPcEbHJ_AexRKNxmqUHL1qYlTLAxx7ViE=
GclCWBVq3Yc5qajTH4QlMnWmzhJKz89ecfpj2cyOIrABLWnuxhMpV2hV8jgDWdJNcYIoyQJmsCa=
Tp3h8dyTBik37urVue2sdtvj4vRg32jujyDegLiXe124pPGLYlrbl6d8SgyeiJTbPven-N8O1vs=
bduNjD624PwKHBBi0QHPeZwu5Y1cLxswEUV1KXzCV3y2LdahnaJobNHXiymi6kXaMTpjJT1Ha7o=
5U3z/4th/4AriXCnnToa2ZVecOt1aVA/h43/h001.6XzS8ei9SDLB2QHc4uDZ_txEVRPJGTm7ld=
tnmk9sJIg" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">vowed retaliation</a> against any coun=
try that took part in the US-led isolation campaign.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Germany, Europe=E2=80=99s biggest economy,=
 grew 0.3% in the second quarter compared with the previous quarter, driven=
 by exports, <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.=
Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR_rh8Fa8qZAaLfQ7Dyt8EExvLQijDk5KfP2-ssyTgb-qLlPchlqgo7Q=
iCcoPu330bD52c_EfE5nikvax397ULT7Fm7A0-5udJyN5NJMh7HbTcy9HCM9mPWa5EGbnm9_99h=
w25SOrYp_AXa-fO-sKaw8KVuFFN1qWhCNIlWguPolTEeHeaMqWlvOWWBfP3jmLq_pCo12krdO6M=
fkILvI8-HdqBatIdjuHoPRb1Eos94Ys/4th/4AriXCnnToa2ZVecOt1aVA/h44/h001.xPzOty1=
xARMASWDZMl8sL_61ibMRvyCTz862xAmbvqo" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">according t=
o official figures</a>. That=E2=80=99s slightly higher than a preliminary e=
stimate of 0.2%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Ruth Brand, president of the Federal Stati=
stical Office, said: =E2=80=9CThe German economy is maintaining the growth =
momentum seen at the start of the year. As in the first quarter, growth was=
 primarily driven by the positive development of exports.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Total exports of goods and services rose 2=
%. And wholesale and retail trade performed much better than expected, whil=
e investment dipped 0.2%.<strong><br><br></strong></p>
